    "field": "Tropical cyclone climatology",
    "problem": "Existing projections of tropical cyclone intensity under global warming often neglect changes in the subsurface ocean, failing to account for an enhanced cooling effect that may suppress future storm intensification.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method using a 3D ocean mixed layer model with initial ocean conditions from 22 climate models to systematically investigate changes in TC-induced ocean cooling and its suppressive impact on tropical cyclone potential intensity under global warming.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate how future subsurface ocean environment changes, projected by climate models, may suppress the intensification of tropical cyclones under global warming through a stronger ocean cooling effect.",
